WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:03.302
-The President is lying
about refugees

00:00:03.302 --> 00:00:06.405
as he and his ex-national
security adviser, John Bolton,

00:00:06.405 --> 00:00:08.774
argue over whether Bolton quit
or was fired.

00:00:08.774 --> 00:00:11.244
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:13.079
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:13.079 --> 00:00:15.348
♪♪

00:00:15.348 --> 00:00:18.084
As we've established before,
Trump's entire political career

00:00:18.084 --> 00:00:20.386
has been built
on racist conspiracy theories

00:00:20.386 --> 00:00:22.355
about immigrants
and people of color.

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:24.190
Today, for example,
it was reported

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:26.225
that the Trump administration
won't give

00:00:26.225 --> 00:00:28.861
temporary protective status
to people from the Bahamas

00:00:28.861 --> 00:00:30.529
who fled Hurricane Dorian.

00:00:30.529 --> 00:00:33.600
And when he was asked about that
on Monday, Trump said this.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.601
-We have to be very careful.

00:00:35.601 --> 00:00:39.272
Everybody needs
totally proper documentation

00:00:39.272 --> 00:00:45.011
because, look, the Bahamas
has some tremendous problems

00:00:45.011 --> 00:00:47.446
with people going to the Bahamas

00:00:47.446 --> 00:00:49.282
that weren't
supposed to be there.

00:00:49.282 --> 00:00:50.683
I don't want to allow people

00:00:50.683 --> 00:00:52.885
that weren't supposed to be
in the Bahamas

00:00:52.885 --> 00:00:55.221
to come into the United States,

00:00:55.221 --> 00:00:59.625
including some very bad people
and some very bad gang members

00:00:59.625 --> 00:01:02.428
and some very, very bad
drug dealers.

00:01:02.428 --> 00:01:05.297
-I'm sorry.
So you think gang members

00:01:05.297 --> 00:01:07.867
and drug dealers
snuck into the Bahamas

00:01:07.867 --> 00:01:10.737
then hid out there
and waited for a hurricane

00:01:10.737 --> 00:01:14.273
so they could eventually
pretend to be refugees

00:01:14.273 --> 00:01:16.175
and sneak into
the United States.

00:01:16.175 --> 00:01:18.310
"Psst! I need to get
this kilo of cocaine

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:19.645
into the United States."

00:01:19.645 --> 00:01:21.213
"No problem.
Just take it to the Bahamas

00:01:21.213 --> 00:01:23.749
and then wait five years."

00:01:23.749 --> 00:01:25.951
The only people who have
ever been in the Bahamas

00:01:25.951 --> 00:01:27.820
who weren't supposed to be
in the Bahamas

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:30.790
are old people
who got on the wrong cruise.

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:33.493
"I thought we were
going to Barbados!"

00:01:33.493 --> 00:01:36.196
Trump has always conflated
immigrants with criminals

00:01:36.196 --> 00:01:38.631
despite the fact
that immigrants commit crimes

00:01:38.631 --> 00:01:41.033
at lower rates
than native-born Americans.

00:01:41.033 --> 00:01:44.304
This is in many ways the central
lie of his political career,

00:01:44.304 --> 00:01:47.073
and he repeated it again
during a rally on Monday,

00:01:47.073 --> 00:01:50.143
even doing some crowd work with
the audience in North Carolina.

00:01:50.143 --> 00:01:52.345
-One of the biggest issues
in this election

00:01:52.345 --> 00:01:54.813
is, in fact, sanctuary cities.

00:01:54.813 --> 00:01:58.684
Sanctuary-city policies
that force prisons and jails

00:01:58.684 --> 00:02:00.152
to release criminal aliens

00:02:00.152 --> 00:02:02.121
directly into
your neighborhoods.

00:02:02.121 --> 00:02:04.657
"Get out. Go ahead.
Go into the neighborhood.

00:02:04.657 --> 00:02:06.825
[ Crowd booing ]
Go into..."

00:02:06.825 --> 00:02:08.394
What's your neighborhood?
Where do you live?

00:02:08.394 --> 00:02:10.530
-Rutherford.
-What?

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:13.565
Rutherford County.

00:02:13.565 --> 00:02:15.635
[ Cheers and applause ]
Okay.

00:02:15.635 --> 00:02:20.639
So, how do you feel about
having them release

00:02:20.639 --> 00:02:24.844
hardened, horrible criminals
into Rutherford County?

00:02:24.844 --> 00:02:26.312
I don't think so.

00:02:26.312 --> 00:02:27.947
-Oh, they're releasing
hardened criminals

00:02:27.947 --> 00:02:29.348
into Rutherford County?

00:02:29.348 --> 00:02:32.051
Are your aides on parole?

00:02:32.051 --> 00:02:33.319
I mean, seriously.

00:02:33.319 --> 00:02:34.520
Now...

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:36.022
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:36.022 --> 00:02:39.792
Now he's -- he's just
making up scary stories.

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:41.894
He should hold his rallies
in the dark

00:02:41.894 --> 00:02:44.097
with a flashlight
under his face.

00:02:44.097 --> 00:02:46.031
He's like a racist Stephen King.

00:02:46.031 --> 00:02:47.534
"Where do you live? Maine?

00:02:47.534 --> 00:02:50.169
How would you like it if they
released clowns into your sewers

00:02:50.169 --> 00:02:52.538
that bit your arms off?"

00:02:52.538 --> 00:02:53.706
In fact, Trump seems to be

00:02:53.706 --> 00:02:55.607
getting more into crowd work
at his rallies

00:02:55.607 --> 00:02:57.844
because after he had asked
people if they'd be cool

00:02:57.844 --> 00:03:00.279
with fictional criminals
rampaging through their streets,

00:03:00.279 --> 00:03:01.513
he polled the audience

00:03:01.513 --> 00:03:03.850
on a very complex, esoteric
policy question,

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:05.985
a question that has vexed
and bedeviled

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:07.419
academics for centuries,

00:03:07.419 --> 00:03:10.155
a question of such import
that it could very well define

00:03:10.155 --> 00:03:13.625
Trump's presidency and this
country for decades to come.

00:03:13.625 --> 00:03:14.693
-What do you like better?

00:03:14.693 --> 00:03:17.063
"Made in America"
or "Made in the U.S.A."?

00:03:17.063 --> 00:03:19.164
Go ahead.

00:03:19.164 --> 00:03:22.868
Wait. Ready?
We'll go "Made in America."

00:03:22.868 --> 00:03:24.337
Then "Made in the U.S.A."

00:03:24.337 --> 00:03:26.839
What do you like better?
"Made in America"?

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:29.809
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:29.809 --> 00:03:31.711
"Made in the U.S.A."

00:03:31.711 --> 00:03:33.646
[ Loud cheers and applause ]

00:03:42.689 --> 00:03:43.956
Okay.

00:03:43.956 --> 00:03:46.225
-[ Chanting ] U.S.A.! U.S.A.!

00:03:46.225 --> 00:03:51.130
U.S.A.! U.S.A.! U.S.A.! U.S.A.!

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:55.167
-So I think we know that answer.

00:03:55.167 --> 00:03:57.570
-That might be
the single dumbest thing

00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:59.338
I've ever seen in...

00:03:59.338 --> 00:04:02.508
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:02.508 --> 00:04:04.944
...in, uh...

00:04:04.944 --> 00:04:07.613
Dumbest thing I've ever seen
in any arena,

00:04:07.613 --> 00:04:10.883
and I'm including the time
the Toronto Raptors mascot

00:04:10.883 --> 00:04:14.153
tried to skate down the stairs
and fell flat on his face.

00:04:14.153 --> 00:04:16.522
[ Laughter ]

00:04:16.522 --> 00:04:21.027
And, honestly, if at any point
this "Closer Look" bums you out,

00:04:21.027 --> 00:04:23.162
just Google "mascot fails."

00:04:23.162 --> 00:04:24.564
It's a lot of fun.

00:04:24.564 --> 00:04:26.465
In fact,
at the end of this segment,

00:04:26.465 --> 00:04:28.767
when it's time for me
to do my little wrap-up

00:04:28.767 --> 00:04:30.569
summarizing how bad
everything is,

00:04:30.569 --> 00:04:32.705
we're just going to put
some mascot fails

00:04:32.705 --> 00:04:34.940
over my shoulder
to keep you entertained.

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:37.142
Before we do that,
that clip right there

00:04:37.142 --> 00:04:39.244
really feels like
Trump in a nutshell.

00:04:39.244 --> 00:04:40.746
False, performative patriotism,

00:04:40.746 --> 00:04:42.481
pretending
he's making decisions,

00:04:42.481 --> 00:04:44.683
when all he really cares about
is branding himself.

00:04:44.683 --> 00:04:46.718
Before that rally,
he was probably up all night

00:04:46.718 --> 00:04:49.488
trying to crack that one
like Mozart writing a symphony.

00:04:49.488 --> 00:04:51.824
"Made in America? No?

00:04:51.824 --> 00:04:53.425
Made in the United States? No.

00:04:53.425 --> 00:04:54.694
Made in the U.S. of A?

00:04:54.694 --> 00:04:57.430
Damn it, Donald.
You can do this!"

00:04:57.430 --> 00:04:59.031
And the same empty symbolism

00:04:59.031 --> 00:05:01.167
is the hallmark
of Trump's foreign policy.

00:05:01.167 --> 00:05:02.602
During the campaign, he lied

00:05:02.602 --> 00:05:04.937
and said he'd been against
the Iraq War from the beginning

00:05:04.937 --> 00:05:07.907
but also called himself the most
militaristic person ever

00:05:07.907 --> 00:05:10.410
and proclaimed his support
for a bunch of war crimes

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:12.278
including torture,
taking Iraq's oil,

00:05:12.278 --> 00:05:14.247
and killing the families
of terrorists.

00:05:14.247 --> 00:05:15.914
And, of course, he famously said

00:05:15.914 --> 00:05:18.417
his main adviser on
foreign policy was himself

00:05:18.417 --> 00:05:21.320
and that he got all his ideas
from watching television.

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:24.089
-Who do you talk to for
military advice right now?

00:05:24.089 --> 00:05:25.624
-Well, I watch the shows.

00:05:25.624 --> 00:05:27.627
I mean,
I really see a lot of great --

00:05:27.627 --> 00:05:29.495
You know,
when you watch your show

00:05:29.495 --> 00:05:30.862
and all of the other shows

00:05:30.862 --> 00:05:33.499
and you have the generals
and you have certain people --

00:05:33.499 --> 00:05:35.868
-But is there somebody --
Is there a go-to for you?

00:05:35.868 --> 00:05:38.937
You know? Every presidential
candidate has a go-to.

00:05:38.937 --> 00:05:40.840
-Probably there are
two or three.

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:43.309
-Since we have some dire
foreign-policy issues

00:05:43.309 --> 00:05:45.444
percolating around the world
right now,

00:05:45.444 --> 00:05:47.713
who are you consulting with
consistently

00:05:47.713 --> 00:05:50.182
so that you're ready on day one?

00:05:50.182 --> 00:05:52.985
-I'm speaking with myself,
number one,

00:05:52.985 --> 00:05:56.689
because I have a very good brain
and I've said a lot of things.

00:05:56.689 --> 00:05:58.090
-Oh, my gosh.

00:05:58.090 --> 00:06:00.993
"I have a very good brain
and I've said a lot of things."

00:06:00.993 --> 00:06:04.396
It sounds like they translated
rap lyrics into Japanese

00:06:04.396 --> 00:06:07.566
and then back into English
with outdated software.

00:06:07.566 --> 00:06:09.401
That sounds like
a tape recording

00:06:09.401 --> 00:06:12.038
a psychological profile
would play during a trial

00:06:12.038 --> 00:06:14.407
where the defendant
is pleading insanity.

00:06:14.407 --> 00:06:17.009
"I heard the defendant having
a conversation in his cell,

00:06:17.009 --> 00:06:20.279
and I asked him who
he was speaking with,
and he said this."

00:06:20.279 --> 00:06:23.049
-I'm speaking with myself,
number one,

00:06:23.049 --> 00:06:27.086
because I have a very good brain
and I've said a lot of things.

00:06:27.086 --> 00:06:30.089
-"Defendant is legally insane.
Court adjourned."

00:06:30.089 --> 00:06:32.191
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:32.191 --> 00:06:34.993
So, Trump says he gets
his foreign-policy advice

00:06:34.993 --> 00:06:36.362
from the shows, and, of course,

00:06:36.362 --> 00:06:38.498
in particular he was talking
about Fox News.

00:06:38.498 --> 00:06:39.966
That's where he saw John Bolton,

00:06:39.966 --> 00:06:42.667
the former Bush administration
official and Fox News pundit

00:06:42.667 --> 00:06:44.136
who Trump hired last year

00:06:44.136 --> 00:06:46.739
as his third national security
adviser, which was horrifying

00:06:46.739 --> 00:06:48.307
because Bolton is
an unrepentant warmonger

00:06:48.307 --> 00:06:51.611
who has pushed for a regime
change in Iraq, Iran, Syria,

00:06:51.611 --> 00:06:53.245
Venezuela, and North Korea.

00:06:53.245 --> 00:06:55.414
In fact, a former Trump
administration official

00:06:55.414 --> 00:06:56.815
actually told "The New Yorker,"

00:06:56.815 --> 00:06:59.117
"John wants to bomb everyone."

00:06:59.117 --> 00:07:01.020
And it's dangerous
to have someone like that

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:03.122
around Donald Trump because
Trump is very impressionable.

00:07:03.122 --> 00:07:05.358
If Marilyn Manson
had a show on Fox News,

00:07:05.358 --> 00:07:07.927
Trump would show up
to his next press conference

00:07:07.927 --> 00:07:11.097
with jet black hair
and a nose ring.

00:07:11.097 --> 00:07:13.999
It was always terrifying knowing
that an extremist neocon

00:07:13.999 --> 00:07:16.435
like Bolton had the ear
of an impressionable president

00:07:16.435 --> 00:07:18.070
who had no idea
what he was doing

00:07:18.070 --> 00:07:19.972
and who took his advice
from TV pundits.

00:07:19.972 --> 00:07:21.707
The relationship
was always weird.

00:07:21.707 --> 00:07:24.410
And yesterday, it came to an end
when Trump fired Bolton.

00:07:24.410 --> 00:07:26.646
Or maybe Bolton quit.
We don't really know

00:07:26.646 --> 00:07:29.414
because, as usual, it happened
in the most chaotic way possible

00:07:29.414 --> 00:07:32.451
with Trump tweeting about it
and Bolton texting reporters

00:07:32.451 --> 00:07:35.955
while they were live on the air
reporting on his firing.

00:07:35.955 --> 00:07:38.924
-Trump announced he'd fired
Bolton this morning on Twitter,

00:07:38.924 --> 00:07:42.228
writing, "I informed John Bolton
last night

00:07:42.228 --> 00:07:45.264
that his services are no longer
needed at the White House."

00:07:45.264 --> 00:07:46.932
-We're just hearing
from Peter Baker

00:07:46.932 --> 00:07:49.035
that John Bolton
has texted him, as well,

00:07:49.035 --> 00:07:53.205
saying that he offered to resign
and resign today.

00:07:53.205 --> 00:07:57.576
So that version
is differing very much

00:07:57.576 --> 00:08:01.113
from the firing version
that comes from the President.

00:08:01.113 --> 00:08:04.550
-John Bolton just texted me.
Just now. He's watching.

00:08:04.550 --> 00:08:06.051
-Can you read it?
-Yeah.

00:08:06.051 --> 00:08:08.854
He said,
"Let's be clear. I resigned."

00:08:08.854 --> 00:08:10.589
And I said,
"Do you mind if I say that?

00:08:10.589 --> 00:08:12.791
while you were talking,
and he wrote, "Yes."

00:08:12.791 --> 00:08:16.429
So John Bolton has just told me,
texted me to say, "I resigned."

00:08:16.429 --> 00:08:18.097
-This is insane.

00:08:18.097 --> 00:08:21.300
They're all talking to each
other through the television.

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:23.668
Trump is firing people
via tweet,

00:08:23.668 --> 00:08:26.672
Bolton is texting news anchors
on live TV to respond.

00:08:26.672 --> 00:08:29.007
It's like if you were
watching a soap opera,

00:08:29.007 --> 00:08:31.610
and in the soap opera,
one of the characters said,

00:08:31.610 --> 00:08:34.346
"Oh, my God, John's evil twin
is at home watching this,

00:08:34.346 --> 00:08:37.416
and he just texted me to say...

00:08:37.416 --> 00:08:39.051
he's alive."

00:08:39.051 --> 00:08:40.786
[ Laughter ]

00:08:40.786 --> 00:08:42.822
[ Applause ]

00:08:46.024 --> 00:08:48.327
Today during a meeting
in the Oval Office

00:08:48.327 --> 00:08:50.295
Trump was asked about
his decision to fire Bolton

00:08:50.295 --> 00:08:52.665
and tried simultaneously
to criticize Bolton

00:08:52.665 --> 00:08:55.067
for his extremist views
while also insisting

00:08:55.067 --> 00:08:56.502
that he was tougher than Bolton,

00:08:56.502 --> 00:08:59.538
but he also specifically and
repeatedly went out of his way

00:08:59.538 --> 00:09:02.207
to criticize Bolton
for his role in the Iraq War.

00:09:02.207 --> 00:09:05.477
-What led you
to decide to part ways?

00:09:05.477 --> 00:09:09.047
-So, John is somebody

00:09:09.047 --> 00:09:11.550
that I actually got along with
very well.

00:09:11.550 --> 00:09:15.187
He made some very big mistakes,

00:09:15.187 --> 00:09:18.357
and, frankly,
he wanted to do things

00:09:18.357 --> 00:09:20.393
not necessarily tougher than me.

00:09:20.393 --> 00:09:21.860
John's known as a tough guy.

00:09:21.860 --> 00:09:23.729
He's so tough,
he got us into Iraq.

00:09:23.729 --> 00:09:26.232
And, you know, John wasn't
in line with what we were doing,

00:09:26.232 --> 00:09:29.067
and actually in some cases
he thought it was too tough

00:09:29.067 --> 00:09:31.003
what we were doing.

00:09:31.003 --> 00:09:33.405
Mr. Tough Guy. You know,
you have to go into Iraq.

00:09:33.405 --> 00:09:35.040
Going into Iraq was something

00:09:35.040 --> 00:09:37.109
that he felt
very strongly about.

00:09:37.109 --> 00:09:39.844
So we're right now in
for over $7 trillion

00:09:39.844 --> 00:09:41.547
into the Middle East.

00:09:41.547 --> 00:09:43.548
But he was very out there,
I can tell you,

00:09:43.548 --> 00:09:45.885
and wanting to have them do it.

00:09:45.885 --> 00:09:47.953
I thought it was
a terrible mistake.

00:09:47.953 --> 00:09:49.488
-If you knew all that then,

00:09:49.488 --> 00:09:51.556
why did you hire him
in the first place?

00:09:51.556 --> 00:09:53.926
This is like firing someone
for embezzlement

00:09:53.926 --> 00:09:56.495
when they had "embezzlement"
under "special skills"

00:09:56.495 --> 00:09:58.263
on their résumé.

00:09:58.263 --> 00:10:00.199
Now, again,
it's absolutely a good thing

00:10:00.199 --> 00:10:02.434
that an extremist warmonger
like Bolton is gone,

00:10:02.434 --> 00:10:05.137
but it's also bad that he was
even hired in the first place.

00:10:05.137 --> 00:10:07.706
So where does this leave us
as a nation?

00:10:07.706 --> 00:10:10.976
Allow me to summarize.
Cue the mascot fails.

00:10:10.976 --> 00:10:13.812
John Bolton
is an unrepentant warmonger

00:10:13.812 --> 00:10:17.382
who was hired by a president
who has no consistent world view

00:10:17.382 --> 00:10:19.885
when it comes to foreign policy,
or anything for that matter.

00:10:19.885 --> 00:10:22.388
All he has are the racist
conspiracy theories

00:10:22.388 --> 00:10:23.856
he concocts in his rotting brain

00:10:23.856 --> 00:10:25.924
and the paranoid
right-wing media apparatus

00:10:25.924 --> 00:10:27.259
that feeds him those theories

00:10:27.259 --> 00:10:29.161
and then disseminates them
to his base.

00:10:29.161 --> 00:10:31.596
Having Bolton in the White House
was a nightmare, but it's

00:10:31.596 --> 00:10:34.366
just as terrifying to imagine
who Trump might hire next.

00:10:34.366 --> 00:10:35.701
I mean, who knows?

00:10:35.701 --> 00:10:38.203
If all he does is hire people
he sees on TV,

00:10:38.203 --> 00:10:41.440
he might as well go ahead
and pick this guy.

00:10:41.440 --> 00:10:43.075
[ Laughter ]

00:10:43.075 --> 00:10:45.778
This has been "A Closer Look."

